# TruthOracle — copy to `.env` and fill in the blanks (the Keycloak client id/secret
# and VITE_ENTERPRISE_WALLET_PARTY_ID).
#
# EVERY VARIABLE THE CODE READS IS LISTED HERE AS AN ACTIVE ENTRY — the browser
# bundle's (frontend/config.ts), the Vercel proxies' (api/) and the native build's
# (capacitor.config.ts). The required ones are listed just below and belong in `.env`
# locally and in the Vercel project environment; the optional ones sit at the default
# the code applies, or blank. A blank value is the same as unset everywhere (every
# reader skips an empty string), so the file can be copied as-is and only the blanks
# that matter filled in. Nothing is commented out: a name missing from this file is
# one nothing reads any more.
# The "Accounts backend" block at the very end (BACKEND_URL, BACKEND_PROXY_SECRET,
# VITE_BACKEND_PROXY_URL, VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, VITE_TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME,
# VITE_TELEGRAM_OIDC_ENABLED) is OPTIONAL as a whole — leave it blank and the app runs
# without accounts: reads and wallet-signed trading only, no deposits or withdrawals
# (those need an account).
#
# Required — frontend + Vercel:
#   VITE_APP_NETWORK                  VITE_CANTON_PARTICIPANT_URL
#   VITE_WALLET_TYPE                  VITE_KEYCLOAK_URL
#   VITE_LOOP_NETWORK                 VITE_KEYCLOAK_REALM
#   VITE_USE_PARTICIPANT_API          KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID
#   VITE_TRUTHORACLE_PACKAGE_ID       KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET
#   VITE_TRUTHORACLE_PACKAGE_NAME     VITE_ENTERPRISE_WALLET_PARTY_ID
#
# Plus the ZKPC_* block — required on a mainnet deployment, where the ledger proxy
# reads it INSTEAD of the digik values above.
#
# The Daml package and the operator scripts (DAR upload, MarketCounter bootstrap,
# ledger queries) moved to the truthoracle-contracts repository, the treasury wallet
# deployment to enterprise-wallet, and accounts/KYC to truthoracle-backend — each has
# its own .env.example.
#
# The two that bite hardest if missed:
#   VITE_ENTERPRISE_WALLET_PARTY_ID — marketplace queries throw, and the ledger relay
#                                     refuses every prepare / execute (fail closed)
#   VITE_CANTON_PARTICIPANT_URL     — market reads/writes 500 "Missing proxy target"
#
# =============================================================================
# FRONTEND + VERCEL — every var in this section is read by the deployed app:
# the browser bundle (frontend/config.ts) and the serverless proxies
# (api/proxy/ledger.mjs). These are the ones to set
# in the Vercel project environment. There is no wallet relay: nothing in the
# browser signs as the treasury (market resolution is the accounts backend's).
#
# The split that matters is not the VITE_ prefix on its own — it is whether
# frontend/config.ts *reads* a name. Vite inlines a VITE_ var into the public JS
# only where it sees an explicit `import.meta.env.VITE_X` reference, so the
# VITE_-named upstream URLs below stay server-side today. Credentials are the
# exception with no judgement call: they never take a VITE_ prefix, and the
# proxies refuse to read one that does.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERCEL: "Secret" vs "Config"
#
# Vercel flags any VITE_-prefixed variable you mark "Secret": "The VITE_ prefix
# exposes this value to the browser." Heed it — it is right about the prefix. What
# to do depends on which group the var is in:
#
# 1. VITE_* that frontend/config.ts reads (APP_NETWORK, WALLET_TYPE, LOOP_NETWORK,
#    USE_PARTICIPANT_API, TRUTHORACLE_PACKAGE_ID/_NAME, ENTERPRISE_WALLET_PARTY_ID
#    — plus the optional accounts-backend ones at the end:
#    BACKEND_PROXY_URL, GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME, TELEGRAM_OIDC_ENABLED)
#    → type "Config". These genuinely are compiled into
#    the public JS. "Secret" hides them from your own dashboard, not from anyone
#    who opens devtools. None of them is sensitive; Config is the honest label.
#
# 2. VITE_* upstream URLs (VITE_CANTON_PARTICIPANT_URL, VITE_KEYCLOAK_URL,
#    VITE_KEYCLOAK_REALM) → on Vercel, set the non-VITE alias
#    instead and mark it "Secret". Same value, no warning, and a name that cannot
#    be inlined even by a later edit to frontend/config.ts:
#       CANTON_LEDGER_PROXY_TARGET_URL      instead of VITE_CANTON_PARTICIPANT_URL
#       KEYCLOAK_URL                        instead of VITE_KEYCLOAK_URL
#       KEYCLOAK_REALM                      instead of VITE_KEYCLOAK_REALM
#    The alias outranks the VITE_ name in the server code (the ledger proxy), so
#    Vercel can carry only the alias. Locally either spelling works.
#
# 3. KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID / KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET, the whole ZKPC_* block, and the
#    accounts-backend pair BACKEND_URL / BACKEND_PROXY_SECRET → "Secret". No VITE_
#    prefix, so no warning.
#
# Rule of thumb: if Vercel warns, either the value is safe to expose (make it
# Config) or you picked the wrong name (switch to the alias in group 2). Do not
# leave a VITE_ var sitting on "Secret" — that combination is only ever misleading.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser (VITE_ prefix, read by frontend/config.ts) — compiled into the public
# JS bundle. In Vercel these are group 1 above: type "Config", NOT "Secret".
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Wallet type: "cantor8" (default) or "canton" (Loop SDK)
VITE_WALLET_TYPE=cantor8

# Network (devnet, testnet, mainnet). On "mainnet" the LEDGER proxy
# (api/proxy/ledger.mjs — create market, active-contracts reads) targets the
# zkpc node and mints tokens from the ZKPC_* block below ONLY. Only "mainnet" is
# special-cased; any other value (including "testnet") behaves as devnet.
VITE_APP_NETWORK=devnet

# Loop wallet network when using canton wallet (local, devnet, testnet, mainnet)
VITE_LOOP_NETWORK=devnet

# TruthOracle DAML package ID on the participant (after DAR upload)
VITE_TRUTHORACLE_PACKAGE_ID=<package id printed by npm run dars:upload in truthoracle-contracts>

# TruthOracle DAML package *name* (daml.yaml `name:` — truthoracle-v17, the package that
# carries a collateral instrument per market and one UserWallet per owner and instrument).
# The JSON Ledger API active-contracts template filter expects a package-name reference
# ("#truthoracle-v17:Module:Entity"), not a package id. Set it together with the package
# id above: the browser falls back to truthoracle-v17, which is wrong for any other version.
VITE_TRUTHORACLE_PACKAGE_NAME=truthoracle-v17

# Participant API vs Loop wallet for transactions in the app
VITE_USE_PARTICIPANT_API=true

# Enterprise Wallet admin party (full party id derived from the wallet's mnemonic).
# Created once with `npm run create:account` in the truthoracle-contracts repository (it
# POSTs to the wallet's /api/v1/accounts — see ../enterprise-wallet/README.md).
# REQUIRED: the UI uses this as the actAs/observer party for active-contracts queries
# (Marketplace, MarketCounter lookup) and as the treasury deposits are sent to. Without
# it the marketplace queries throw. The ledger relay (server-side) reads it too: it
# refuses an interactive submission (prepare / execute) acting or reading as this party,
# and every one while it is unset. The same value goes in truthoracle-contracts/.env
# and in truthoracle-backend/.env (TREASURY_PARTY_ID).
VITE_ENTERPRISE_WALLET_PARTY_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream URLs — read via process.env by api/proxy/*.mjs,
# NOT by frontend/config.ts. The browser only ever talks to /__proxy/*, so it
# never needs these; they are named VITE_* purely because Vite must expose them
# to the dev server, and nothing reads them into the bundle.
#
# Each has a non-VITE alias that the PROXIES prefer if you set it — use those on
# Vercel (see the Secret/Config note above):
#   CANTON_LEDGER_PROXY_TARGET_URL      over VITE_CANTON_PARTICIPANT_URL
#   KEYCLOAK_URL / KEYCLOAK_REALM       over VITE_KEYCLOAK_URL / VITE_KEYCLOAK_REALM
#
# The aliases are a Vercel convenience ONLY. Locally either spelling works for the
# proxies. (The operator scripts that used to read the VITE_ names now live in the
# truthoracle-contracts repository with their own .env — see its .env.example.)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Canton Ledger API base URL — the target api/proxy/ledger.mjs forwards to
# (prepare/execute, active-contracts), and the ledger endpoint the Node scripts
# call directly on `--network devnet`.
VITE_CANTON_PARTICIPANT_URL=https://api.validator.dev.digik.cantor8.tech/api/ledger

# Keycloak issuer for the Ledger API and the Node scripts.
# _keycloakToken.mjs resolves it as the "VITE_KEYCLOAK"/"KEYCLOAK" prefix when
# minting client_credentials tokens. Tokens are minted SERVER-SIDE only — by the
# proxies and the scripts, never in the browser (there is no user-auth passthrough).
VITE_KEYCLOAK_URL=https://auth.dev.digik.cantor8.tech
VITE_KEYCLOAK_REALM=master

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials (NO VITE_ prefix, ever) — the client_credentials pair the proxies and
# scripts use against the Keycloak above. A VITE_-prefixed spelling of these two
# names is deliberately IGNORED by api/proxy/_keycloakToken.mjs and by the scripts,
# so a stray VITE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET cannot become the live credential.
# In Vercel: type "Secret".
#
# These are the digik (devnet) credentials. The zkpc (MainNet) node has its OWN
# client — the ZKPC_* block below. Scripts pick exactly one set via --network and
# never fall back to the other network's values.
# The accounts backend (truthoracle-backend) mints its own tokens from its own .env;
# nothing in this block changes when it is deployed.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id
KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret

# =============================================================================
# zkpc (MainNet) node — used by the app's LEDGER proxy when VITE_APP_NETWORK=mainnet
# (create market, active-contracts reads). (The operator scripts that also read
# this block — dars:upload, contracts:active, ledger:query, rights:grant — now live in
# the truthoracle-contracts repository with their own .env.)
# Nothing here changes for the accounts backend either — it carries its own ledger
# and Keycloak config in truthoracle-backend/.env.
# =============================================================================
# Admin Ledger API + Keycloak credentials for the dedicated Cantor8 zkpc node.
# These are DIFFERENT credentials from the digik set above — a script on zkpc reads
# ONLY the ZKPC_* values (and vice versa), so a missing value fails fast instead of
# silently authenticating against the wrong Keycloak. All server-only. Client id and
# secret are shared by Cantor8 in DM.
ZKPC_LEDGER_API_URL=https://api.validator.main.zkpc.cantor8.tech/api/ledger
ZKPC_KEYCLOAK_URL=https://auth.main.zkpc.cantor8.tech
ZKPC_KEYCLOAK_REALM=master
ZKPC_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=
ZKPC_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=

# =============================================================================
# Optional overrides — each at the default the code applies, or blank (= unset)
# =============================================================================

# Dev: "true" logs active-contracts lookups in the browser console.
VITE_DEBUG_ACTIVE_CONTRACTS=false

# Dev: "true" logs Cantor8 wallet status probes.
VITE_DEBUG_WALLET_STATUS=false

# Dev: "true" keeps the developer narration (wallet popup messages, signAndExecute
# inputs, committed tx hashes — frontend/lib/debugLog.ts) in a PRODUCTION build, to
# debug a live issue. `vite dev` prints it regardless; warnings and errors always print.
VITE_DEBUG_WALLET=false

# Browser → proxy path. Change only if the /__proxy/ledger route in vercel.json moves.
VITE_CANTON_PARTICIPANT_PROXY_URL=/__proxy/ledger

# Non-VITE aliases for the upstream URLs above. Set one and the server code
# prefers it over the VITE_ counterpart. Same
# values as the VITE_ names — on DevNet that is
#   CANTON_LEDGER_PROXY_TARGET_URL=https://api.validator.dev.digik.cantor8.tech/api/ledger
#   KEYCLOAK_URL=https://auth.dev.digik.cantor8.tech
#   KEYCLOAK_REALM=master
# — the difference is that the name can never be inlined into the bundle, even by a
# future edit to frontend/config.ts. Blank = the VITE_ name applies. The Node scripts
# do NOT read these — see the note in the upstream-URL section above.
CANTON_LEDGER_PROXY_TARGET_URL=
KEYCLOAK_URL=
KEYCLOAK_REALM=

# Optional: a SEPARATE confidential client for the ledger proxy only. If set, the
# proxy prefers these over the shared credentials above.
#
# Grepping the source for "LEDGER_KEYCLOAK_URL" (or any full name in this block)
# finds nothing — that is expected, not dead config. api/proxy/ledger.mjs passes a
# PREFIX list to keycloakBearer() (["LEDGER_KEYCLOAK", "KEYCLOAK", "VITE_KEYCLOAK"])
# and _keycloakToken.mjs composes `${prefix}_${suffix}` at runtime. Grep for the
# prefix instead. Same goes for the ZKPC_KEYCLOAK_* block above.
#
# LEDGER_KEYCLOAK_* is read by api/proxy/ledger.mjs on non-mainnet networks.
# URL/REALM fall back to the shared values (so https://auth.dev.digik.cantor8.tech /
# master need not be repeated); CLIENT_ID/SECRET do not. Blank = the proxy uses the
# shared credentials.
LEDGER_KEYCLOAK_URL=
LEDGER_KEYCLOAK_REALM=
LEDGER_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=
LEDGER_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=

# =============================================================================
# iOS / CAPACITOR BUILD ONLY — read by capacitor.config.ts when building the
# native shell. Not read by the browser bundle or the Vercel proxies.
# =============================================================================

# iOS Capacitor hosted mode: the app's hosted web origin (e.g. https://beta.truthoracle.xyz).
# Blank (as in the checked-in .env) the shell serves the bundled dist/ instead.
CAPACITOR_SERVER_URL=

# "true" points the native shell at the local dev server (http://localhost:5173)
# while CAPACITOR_SERVER_URL is blank.
CAPACITOR_DEV_SERVER=false


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin authentication  (see ADMIN_AUTH.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY — no VITE_ prefix. Vite compiles every referenced VITE_* var into the
# public JS bundle, so a VITE_-prefixed secret here would ship to every visitor.
#
# Without ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET the privileged proxy paths fail CLOSED (503): admin
# actions are disabled for everyone rather than open to everyone.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# Operators permitted to hold an admin session, as <partyId>=<publicKey> pairs,
# comma separated. The public key is PINNED here on purpose — it is what the login
# signature is checked against, so it must never come from the browser.
# Key may be hex, base64 or base64url; it is identified by decoding to 32 bytes.
# The key is the Ed25519 public key on the wallet's account payload (see
# ADMIN_AUTH.md for how to read it).
#
# ADMIN_OPERATORS="a99dd107…::1220880b…=b6f1…,3b9317d2…::1220514795…=9ac4…"
ADMIN_OPERATORS=

# Optional. Admin session lifetime in hours (default 0.25 = 15 minutes; max 24).
# Absolute, not sliding — activity never extends a session. Re-auth is one popup.
ADMIN_SESSION_TTL_HOURS=0.25

# Optional, server-only: override the Cantor8 wallet-backend the /__proxy/c8b relay
# forwards to. Blank = per-network default (VITE_APP_NETWORK=mainnet →
# wallet-backend.main.digik.cantor8.tech, else wallet-backend.dev.digik.cantor8.tech).
# The relay exists because the mainnet backend sends no CORS headers; the browser
# calls /__proxy/c8b with the user's own bearer (no server credential involved).
C8_WALLET_BACKEND_URL=

# Optional, frontend: where the app reaches the wallet-backend. Default is the
# same-origin relay path — only change this if you know the backend allows CORS
# for your origin (e.g. local experiments against devnet directly).
VITE_C8_BACKEND_URL=/__proxy/c8b

# Optional but recommended: an Upstash-compatible Redis REST endpoint makes the
# admin nonce single-use guard and login rate limit FLEET-WIDE instead of
# per-serverless-instance. Vercel KV exposes exactly the KV_* pair when attached;
# plain Upstash uses the UPSTASH_* pair. Both pairs are honoured, KV_* first
# (api/_lib/sharedStore.mjs). Blank = the guards degrade to per-instance, never fail.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accounts backend  (truthoracle-backend — sign-in, linked wallets, KYC, in-app
# wallet; see ../truthoracle-backend/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §4.1 and §16)
#
# ALL OPTIONAL, but BACKEND_URL is what enables deposits and withdrawals: the backend
# is the only thing that credits or settles an in-app UserWallet (deposit attribution
# across an account's linked wallets, KYC-gated payouts). With it blank the app has no
# accounts — no Sign-in button, no deposit/withdraw controls — and is read + wallet-
# signed trading only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SERVER-ONLY (Vercel: "Secret"; no VITE_ prefix, ever). Absolute URL of the backend
# — the Railway service, e.g. https://truthoracle-backend.up.railway.app. Must start
# with http(s)://; anything else is treated as unset. The browser never sees it: it
# calls the same-origin relay /__backend/* (api/proxy/backend.mjs), which forwards
# here. Blank = accounts disabled.
BACKEND_URL=

# SERVER-ONLY (Vercel: "Secret"). Must EQUAL the backend's BACKEND_PROXY_SECRET. Sent
# as x-truthoracle-proxy on every relayed request; only when it matches does the
# backend trust the relay's x-forwarded-host (app host, for cookies / CSRF / the
# wallet challenge message) and x-real-ip (client IP, for rate limits). Without it
# the backend falls back to the relay's own address for every visitor.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
BACKEND_PROXY_SECRET=

# Browser (VITE_ prefix, read by frontend/config.ts; Vercel: "Config", NOT "Secret").
# Each is optional on its own, but Google and Telegram are the ONLY sign-in methods (the
# Cantor8 wallet is linked to the account afterwards, never a sign-in method), so a
# deployment with neither VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID nor VITE_TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME lets
# nobody sign in, deposit or trade.

# Where the app reaches the backend. Default is the same-origin relay path; change
# it only together with the /__backend rewrite in vercel.json.
VITE_BACKEND_PROXY_URL=/__backend

# Google Identity Services client id (the "Web application" OAuth client). Blank =
# no Google button. The same id must be in the backend's GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Telegram bot username (without "@") whose domain is set with BotFather for the
# Login Widget. Blank = Telegram sign-in hidden.
VITE_TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=

# "true" only on hosts whose https://<host>/__backend/api/v1/auth/telegram/oidc/callback
# is registered with Telegram; adds the OIDC button next to the widget.
VITE_TELEGRAM_OIDC_ENABLED=false
